gdn-fused-conv-l2norm.patch  (notes/hardware-spark.md, proposal P5; claim C122; check SQ77)

Opt-in: model config "gdn_fused_kernels": true makes each GDN layer use kernels fla 0.6.0 already ships:
  * the short causal convs run through fla's Triton causal_conv1d with SiLU fused (one kernel instead of
    transpose + cuDNN depthwise conv + slice + transpose + SiLU, fwd and bwd), same [C, 1, K] weights, so
    state_dict keys and checkpoints are unchanged;
  * q/k L2 normalisation moves inside chunk_gated_delta_rule (use_qk_l2norm_in_kernel=True; eps 1e-6 inside the
    kernel vs F.normalize's 1e-12 clamp, so numerics differ in the last bits).
Default false = current behaviour, bit-identical. Apply after SQ77 passes:
git apply notes/patches/gdn-fused-conv-l2norm.patch

--- a/gogeta/model.py
+++ b/gogeta/model.py
